{"number": 76, "text": "           Exercises\n\n                   Report what was said, quoting the speaker’s exact words using one of the reporting verbs from\n                   the box. Put the reporting clause after the quotation and give alternative word orders where\n                   possible.\n                     boast    chorus    -command       confess               grumble      suggest    wonder\n\n                   1 Come  in out of the rain now. (her mother)\n                       ‘Come. in out of the rain now,’  commanded   her mother  / her mother  commanded.\n                     Why  don’t we stop for a coffee? (she)\n                   Nn\n                     All right, Georgia, it was me. (he)\n                     My  novel is more exciting than a Dan Brown thriller. (she)\n                     | always carry two umbrellas with me because I’m always losing them. (Lena)\n                     Oh, no, it’s raining again. (Matt)\n                     Good  morning, Miss Novak. (the children)\n                     Have | done the right thing? (/)\n\n                    omplete  each sentence using a pair of verbs from the box. Make one of the verbs negative.\n                    announce-go                                      -intend—hurt-\n                                | promise-would       think-would       threaten-repay\n                  1          mean to upset Astrid.’      didn’t intend. to hurt.  her feelings.\n                  2  ‘| won't give you the money back if you keep on at me.’ — He                       the\n                     money  if she kept on at him.\n                  3  ‘I can’t ask my parents to help me again.’ >             that he..........    ask his\n                     parents to help him again.\n                  4   wasn’t anywhere  near the school at the time of the break-in.’ >           . that he\n                                  anywhere  near the school at the time of the break-in.\n                  5  ‘I'm not going back to college.’ — She.         that she              back to college.\n                  6   was  surprised that Mum was angry.’  He              His Mother .......\n                  7  ‘Adam won't mind waiting.”  She                                  Mind waiting.\n                  8   won't be late again.’ She............................. that she ..... ...be late again.\n                  Complete  the email by reporting these questions using a wh-, if- or whether-clause.\n                            lid               hejob2!\n                  2  ‘What  are your long-term career plans?’\n                  3  ‘How  many  languages do you speak?’\n                  4  ‘Where did you learn Chinese?’\n                  5  ‘Can you use a spreadsheet?’\n                  6  ‘Have you organised international conferences before?’\n                  7  ‘Would you be willing to live overseas for periods of time?’\n                  8  ‘When  can you start work?’\n                                                                                2                         ©\n            Hi Karim,\n\n            (1)           heard. about  the job,  and then they asked me (2)\n            They were very interested in the travelling I’d done. They asked me (3)\n            and they wondered  (4)                                  « There were questions about my previous\n            experience. They wanted to know (5)                                         and they asked me\n            (6)                                 . At the end they asked (7)\n                                       . When I said ‘Yes’, they asked me (8)                              !\n            I'll phone later and tell you more about it.\n            Emily\n\n\n                                                                                                                65", "char_count": 3813, "mean_conf": 82.91, "word_count": 469, "words": [{"text": "Exercises", "x0": 213, "y0"